  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">Spikes in hybrid attacks (especially cyber intrusions and sabotage) create immediate national security and infrastructure integrity concerns that prompt Chinese regulators to tighten AI, cybersecurity and infrastructure rules and compliance requirements.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">china_tech_push</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::hybrid_attack_intensity" target="energy_supply_shift::maritime_incident_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">An uptick in coordinated kinetic and covert operations increases the use of maritime-targeted sabotage (mines, drones, small-boat attacks and covert seizures), directly raising the frequency and intensity of interdiction incidents in chokepoints.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">energy_supply_shift</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::hybrid_attack_intensity" target="global_bond_shock::bond_fund_net_flows" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">Escalating hybrid operations (cyber strikes, sabotage, localized kinetic) elevate short‑term risk aversion and safe‑haven demand, prompting reallocations into government and high‑quality bond funds and producing net inflows into bond products.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_shock</data>
</edge>
