<edge source="global_bond_shock::nominal_long_yield" target="china_tech_push::ai_investment_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.85</data>
  <data key="d36">A sustained rise in long-term yields raises discount rates and borrowing costs for multi‑year infrastructure projects and increases the hurdle for equity returns, causing Chinese firms and investors to scale back new capital commitments into AI data centres, specialised hardware and long‑lead R&amp;D.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">china_tech_push</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_shock::nominal_long_yield" target="energy_supply_shift::fuel_price_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">A sharp rise in long-term sovereign yields increases financing and hedging costs for traders, refiners and ship operators, which is often passed through into higher spot and wholesale refined-fuel prices in the short term as carrying and working-capital costs rise.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">energy_supply_shift</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_shock::nominal_long_yield" target="russia_ukraine_war::defence_procurement_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">Rising long-term sovereign yields increase government borrowing costs and debt-service burdens, forcing near-term budget re-prioritization and delaying or scaling back defence procurement contracts.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_shock::nominal_long_yield" target="us_iran_hostilities::financial_market_volatil" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.9</data>
  <data key="d36">A rise in long-term yields forces rapid repricing of equities, credit and rate-sensitive assets, triggering margin calls and widening bid-ask spreads that increase realized and expected cross‑market volatility.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_hostilities</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_shock::nominal_long_yield" target="us_iran_hostilities::oil_price_level" id="0">
