<edge source="global_bond_shock::cross_border_capflow_rat" target="global_bond_shock::investor_risk_appetite" id="0">
  <data key="d27">intra_causal</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_shock::cross_border_capflow_rat" target="china_tech_push::chip_prod_capacity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">A drop in cross‑border capital flows into manufacturing and FDI reduces foreign equity, loans and supplier finance available for new fabs and tooling in China, slowing chip‑production line startups and capacity expansion that depend on external financing and inputs.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">china_tech_push</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_shock::cross_border_capflow_rat" target="energy_supply_shift::tanker_traffic_vol" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Rapid net outflows of cross-border capital reduce availability of short-term trade finance and letters-of-credit for exporters and traders, causing shipment delays, cancellations and therefore lower tanker loadings/transits through chokepoints.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">energy_supply_shift</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_shock::cross_border_capflow_rat" target="energy_supply_shift::alt_supply_ramp_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Sustained declines in cross-border capital inflows tighten external financing for upstream operators and service contractors, slowing the pace at which alternative or marginal crude sources can be developed and exported.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">energy_supply_shift</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_shock::cross_border_capflow_rat" target="russia_ukraine_war::alliance_cohesion_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Sudden net capital outflows from allied economies tighten domestic financing conditions and raise political pressure to divert resources from external commitments, reducing willingness to coordinate financing and burden-sharing among partners.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
