<edge source="energy_supply_shift::tanker_traffic_vol" target="energy_supply_shift::freight_insurance_premia" id="0">
  <data key="d27">intra_causal</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
</edge>
<edge source="energy_supply_shift::tanker_traffic_vol" target="china_tech_push::chip_prod_capacity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Changes in tanker traffic through chokepoints alter timely delivery of specialty chemicals, high‑purity gases, cooling fluids and diesel backup fuel and equipment for fabs, so reduced tanker flows directly force wafer fabs to cut runs or delay ramp‑ups while restored/increased flows raise chip production throughput.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">energy_supply_shift</data>
  <data key="d39">china_tech_push</data>
</edge>
<edge source="energy_supply_shift::tanker_traffic_vol" target="us_iran_hostilities::oil_price_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">A sustained rise in tanker throughput increases effective crude delivery capacity to markets, easing short‑term supply tightness and exerting downward pressure on benchmark crude prices.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">energy_supply_shift</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_hostilities</data>
</edge>
